        "procedure": "Ammonium ceric nitrate (550 mg, 1.003 mmol) and benzoic acid (225 mg, 1.842 mmol) were dissolved in 10 mL of pyridine, followed by addition of 8.1 μL of methanol. After stirring for 30 min, the suspension was centrifuged and unreacted residue discarded. The solution was transferred into a 25 mL colorimetric tube and layered with 20 mL of acetonitrile. After standing undisturbed in the dark for 2 weeks, yellow crystals of 1 were obtained (yield 4.4% based on Ce), with some unknown powder precipitated.",
